# Faker Data Generation Project-Specific Rules

## Data Volume and Scaling
- MUST generate data volumes matching project targets (5M-10M customers, 20M-50M orders)
- MUST implement batch processing for large-scale generation to prevent memory issues
- MUST use appropriate batch sizes (10K-100K records per batch) based on available memory
- MUST implement progress tracking and checkpointing for long-running generation jobs
- MUST support incremental data generation for testing and development

## E-Commerce Domain Data
- MUST generate realistic customer demographics with geographic distribution
- MUST implement product categorization with realistic pricing and inventory levels
- MUST generate order data with temporal patterns (peak hours, seasonal trends)
- MUST create payment data with realistic success/failure rates and payment methods
- MUST ensure referential integrity between customers, products, orders, and payments

## Data Distribution and Skew
- MUST implement Pareto principle (80/20 rule) for popular products and high-value customers
- MUST generate realistic customer lifetime value distributions
- MUST create seasonal and temporal patterns in order data
- MUST implement geographic distribution patterns for customers and orders
- MUST ensure data skew matches real e-commerce patterns

## Data Quality and Validation
- MUST validate generated data against business rules (e.g., order dates after customer creation)
- MUST implement data quality checks during generation process
- MUST ensure no orphaned records in related entities
- MUST validate data ranges (prices, quantities, dates) against realistic bounds
- MUST implement duplicate detection and prevention

## Performance and Optimization
- MUST optimize Faker usage with provider caching for repeated data generation
- MUST implement parallel processing for independent data generation tasks
- MUST use appropriate data structures for efficient batch processing
- MUST implement memory-efficient streaming for large dataset generation
- MUST optimize file I/O operations for output formats

## Configuration and Flexibility
- MUST support configurable data volumes for different environments (dev, test, prod)
- MUST allow customization of data distributions and patterns
- MUST support different output formats (CSV, JSON, Parquet) with appropriate compression
- MUST implement environment-specific configurations for data generation
- MUST provide sensible defaults while allowing customization

## Testing and Development Support
- MUST support smaller dataset generation for development and testing
- MUST implement deterministic data generation for reproducible test scenarios
- MUST provide data validation tools for generated datasets
- MUST support data generation with known quality issues for testing data quality checks
- MUST implement data generation metrics and reporting